Release milestone: API freeze, docs, SemVer, PyPI. Owner decisions 2026-10-16: distribution name `openpptx`
(the PyPI name `pypptx` is an unrelated 2015 project; the import stays `pptx`), and a complete rebrand, the
repo included (`RorySullivan1/openpptx`); the contract is the
documented surface (oxml/opc/parts are internal, not renamed); docs on GitHub Pages; the LICENSE carries
python-pptx's notice. Detail is in the card, `.meta/roadmap/stages/04-stable-release/v1.0.0.md`.

## Goals
- Ship as `openpptx`: renamed distribution, full metadata, root LICENSE with python-pptx's notice.
- Public API contract: audit the API layer, stability and deprecation page, public-name snapshot test,
  `DeprecationWarning` shims for anything renamed.
- Docs: guides per area, migration guide from python-pptx, CHANGELOG back to v0.1.0, Pages deploy.
- Release pipeline: Trusted Publishing on a `v*` tag; `1.0.0rc1` first, then `1.0.0`.

## Objectives / acceptance
- [ ] CI green on 7 cells (suite, corpus, examples, work-count gate); coverage ≥ the branch-start baseline.
- [ ] `sphinx-build -W -E` clean; Pages serves the reference, guides, stability page and migration guide.
- [ ] sdist and wheel `openpptx` carry LICENSE with both notices; `twine check` passes; the built wheel runs
      every example on 3.9 and 3.13.
- [ ] The public-API snapshot test passes; each deprecated alias warns and has a test.
- [ ] PowerPoint 16 opens every example's output without repair.
- [ ] `pip install openpptx==1.0.0rc1` works from PyPI (owner-run); migration guide reviewed (human-gated).
